{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(e) => {\n      e.preventDefault()\n      e.stopPropagation()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <div>\n      <form.Field name=\"fullName\">\n        {#snippet children(field)}\n          <input\n            name={field.name}\n            value={field.state.value}\n            onblur={field.handleBlur}\n            oninput={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}\n          />\n        {/snippet}\n      </form.Field>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n  </form>\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!"}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet.\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(e) => {\n      e.preventDefault()\n      e.stopPropagation()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <div>\n      <form.Field name=\"fullName\">\n        {#snippet children(field)}\n          <input\n            name={field.name}\n            value={field.state.value}\n            onblur={field.handleBlur}\n            oninput={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}\n          />\n        {/snippet}\n      </form.Field>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\nFrom here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nThe bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet.\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(e) => {\n      e.preventDefault()\n      e.stopPropagation()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <div>\n      <form.Field name=\"fullName\">\n        {#snippet children(field)}\n          <input\n            name={field.name}\n            value={field.state.value}\n            onblur={field.handleBlur}\n            oninput={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}\n          />\n        {/snippet}\n      </form.Field>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\nFrom here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!\n"}
